  "body": "SslPrincipalMapper.Rule.apply checks the rule with Matcher.matches() but\nthen builds the principal with String.replaceAll, which scans the DN\nagain and can use a different match. For some rules (unanchored, or with\nalternation) this gives a wrong name, e.g. \"bobeng\" instead of \"bob\", or\nthe replacement applied twice.\n\nBuild the name from the same match with Matcher.appendReplacement. A\nrule that produces an empty name is now treated as not matching, so the\nnext rule applies, the same way an invalid result is handled for\nKerberos rules.\n\nAdded unit tests in SslPrincipalMapperTest.\n\nReviewers: Manikumar Reddy <manikumar@confluent.io>\n",
