    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "Aashish Kumar",
     "email": "aaskumar@confluent.io",
     "date": "2026-10-29T07:27:47Z"
    },
    "message": "MINOR: derive SSL principal from the matched groups in SslPrincipalMapper\n\nSslPrincipalMapper.Rule.apply checks the rule with Matcher.matches() but then\nbuilds the principal with String.replaceAll, which scans the DN again and can\nuse a different match. For some rules (unanchored, or with alternation) this\ngives a wrong name, e.g. \"bobeng\" instead of \"bob\", or the replacement\napplied twice.\n\nBuild the name from the same match with Matcher.appendReplacement. A rule that\nproduces an empty name is now treated as not matching, so the next rule\napplies, the same way an invalid result is handled for Kerberos rules.\n\nAdded unit tests in SslPrincipalMapperTest.",
