     "sha": "52ed41b1be6657eed5cb02de95b4c8fcf1e057b7",
     "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/git/trees/52ed41b1be6657eed5cb02de95b4c8fcf1e057b7"
    },
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/git/commits/f191443bee5511ca3503dbe9924184c04a41369e",
    "comment_count": 0,
    "verification": {
     "verified": true,
     "reason": "valid",
     "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgmbGPzS49aG9JuxTpUntOXUKoS8\nE+ot6vddqGtSCvLBcAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNDUp8ACznFNqAHLboUPDGAJBTf30w5Bs9rCqAlpLfrAXuDQLBvKYW/3ree+qje8hP\nPNtHDq/af0Fuskp3zzOAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
     "payload": "tree 52ed41b1be6657eed5cb02de95b4c8fcf1e057b7\nparent a589c272c1666724af8bf137bf1fda1e2b568ef4\nauthor Aashish Kumar <aaskumar@confluent.io> 1793258867 +0530\ncommitter Aashish Kumar <aaskumar@confluent.io> 1793258867 +0530\n\nMINOR: derive SSL principal from the matched groups in SslPrincipalMapper\n\nSslPrincipalMapper.Rule.apply checks the rule with Matcher.matches() but then\nbuilds the principal with String.replaceAll, which scans the DN again and can\nuse a different match. For some rules (unanchored, or with alternation) this\ngives a wrong name, e.g. \"bobeng\" instead of \"bob\", or the replacement\napplied twice.\n\nBuild the name from the same match with Matcher.appendReplacement. A rule that\nproduces an empty name is now treated as not matching, so the next rule\napplies, the same way an invalid result is handled for Kerberos rules.\n\nAdded unit tests in SslPrincipalMapperTest.\n",
